{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0017417","label":"renal-hepatic-pancreatic dysplasia","definition":"A rare, genetic, developmental defect during embryogenesis syndrome characterized by the triad of pancreatic fibrosis (and cysts, with a reduction of parenchymal tissue), renal dysplasia (with peripheral cortical cysts, primitive collecting ducts, glomerular cysts and metaplastic cartilage) and hepatic dysgenesis (enlarged portal areas containing numerous elongated binary profiles with a tendency to perilobular fibrosis). Situs abnormalities, skeletal anomalies and anencephaly have also been associated. Patients that survive the neonatal period present renal insufficiency, chronic jaundice and insulin-dependant diabetes.","synonyms":["Ivemark II syndrome","Renohepaticopancreatic dysplasia"],"xrefs":["DOID:0060259","GARD:0017356","MEDGEN:382215","OMIMPS:208540","Orphanet:294415","SCTID:763891005","UMLS:C2673883"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":2,"n_phenotypes":34,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_0a3abe732f47","source":"MONDO:0017417","target":"NEK8","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:294415","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/294415","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (loss of function) in (Assessed) — NIMA related kinase 8"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:294415","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:294415","snippet":"NEK8 is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:294415 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},{"id":"e_e7bfc7298b01","source":"MONDO:0017417","target":"NPHP3","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:294415","level":"